# HG changeset patch
# User Betterbird <betterbird@betterbird.eu> and DeekSeek
# Date 1789935161 -7200
# Parent  2c898681471c7ead23fa1abcced23ea71625ab72
Feature: Linux systray. Implement context menu with "Quit Betterbird" to match Windows functionality.

  Serve the context menu over com.canonical.dbusmenu:
  Export the GMenu set via app_indicator_set_menu() over dbusmenu, the protocol KDE/Xfce/
  GNOME-Shell-ext actually read.
  
  Patch libayatana-appindicator-glib which exports its menu only via org.gtk.Menus, which
  most hosts do not understand.
  
  Small variation for Mate using a GtkMenu.
* * *
Initial version by Github User mfschumann <github@mfs.name> and Kilo Code:
Feature: Linux systray. Avoid DBusError "No such interface 'com.canonical.dbusmenu'".

  Serve an empty com.canonical.dbusmenu on the indicator object, so
  StatusNotifierItem hosts that only implement the legacy dbusmenu protocol
  (notably the GNOME Shell AppIndicator extension) stop logging
    Gio.DBusError: ... UnknownMethod: No such interface 'com.canonical.dbusmenu'
    of the object at path /org/ayatana/appindicator/Betterbird_systray_icon

